A1. A valuable asset for contractors. ~ ACE
A4. What a man falls back on when he has tire trouble. ~ COT
A7. Shillings and pence. ~ LBS
A10. Even during the depression you could make a fortune out of this. ~ LOTS
A12. The chip on Carnera's shoulder. ~ BOARD
A14. A corn grower. ~ BOOT
A15. This fellow will give you the lowdown on the race. ~ TOUT
A16. A flaw on a diamond. ~ ERROR
A17. This is always getting in the soup. ~ OCRA
A18. Dopes. ~ OPIATES
A20. Overhead in the White House. ~ CEILING
A22. The way the girls are backed to-day. ~ BARE
A23. What people do to have overnight guests. ~ HATE
A24. The guy who puts you on the blink. ~ OCULIST
A27. A precious stone. ~ EMERALD
A31. You can't say that this doesn't try. ~ PANEL
A32. A steady grinder. ~ MOLAR
A33. This is just half decent. ~ ENT
A34. The end of all cheese. ~ ESE
A35. This is what mother got from the children for Christmas. ~ NOISE
A38. Here is where you get the sac. ~ BURSA
A40. A good mixer. ~ SELTZER
A43. This man usually has a lot on his mind. ~ REALTOR
A45. To force onward. ~ URGE
A46. Boarding house victuals. ~ EATS
A47. This is just offal. ~ GARBAGE
A50. What some men do to be successful. ~ PRETEND
A54. This fellow is sure to get a lift from a camel. ~ ARAB
A55. A watchword. ~ ELGIN
A57. The cry of the stag at eve. ~ EVOE
A58. This will put an end to Tammany. ~ MANY
A59. Collegiate conductors. ~ DEANS
A60. Get up! ~ RISE
A61. An order man. ~ ELK
A62. How blondes get that way. ~ DYE
A63. Pulled around by the nose. ~ LED

D1. This was voiced by the lowest female. ~ ALTO
D2. A cagey affair. ~ COOP
D3. You can make a case out of this one. ~ ETUI
D4. This is usually hanging around the women. ~ CORSET
D5. This is always getting into a row. ~ OAR
D6. And this gets down in the mouth at a cold. ~ TROCHE
D7. The way the Romans used to get places. ~ LOCI
D8. A stubborn ending. ~ BORN
D9. They never have chickens at this kind of dinner. ~ STAG
D11. You're apt to get stalled here. ~ STABLE
D12. These froth at the mouth. ~ BEERS
D13. A sleepy time thought. ~ DREAM
D14. This makes the Spaniards step around. ~ BOLERO
D19. The end of the English bull. ~ TAIL
D21. This one is a little particular. ~ ITEM
D24. The first thing a beautician does to her eyes in the morning. ~ OPENS
D25. This makes many tips during the summer. ~ CANOE
D26. 'Til we meet again. ~ UNTIL
D28. Always on the watch. ~ ALERT
D29. This gets tight on a horse's neck. ~ LASSO
D30. That Blue Monday feeling. ~ DREAR
D36. How a woman's check book looks at the end of the month. ~ STUBBY
D37. A man's name. ~ EZRA
D38. The end of a reprobate. ~ BATE
D39. This goes over big in the winter. ~ ULSTER
D41. A thing that ham actors don't like to be. ~ EGGED
D42. Was in a whirl. ~ REELED
D43. To complain in a big way. ~ REPINE
D44. What a woman does to every cent she gets. ~ EARNS
D47. You can play around with this. ~ GAME
D48. A Russian sea. ~ ARAL
D49. This is positively putrid. ~ RANK
D51. And this is positively bad. ~ EVIL
D52. A cold storage compartment. ~ NOSE
D53. This is an act in itself. ~ DEED
D56. One way to get merry. ~ GAY


